variableSuggest.projectMapFunctions.markdownDescription:
Reverse-lookup config. Applies to every open project — no workspace folder name to match. Each entry flattens a (possibly nested) SCSS map — `$<variable>` — into its leaf values, so typing a literal that matches a leaf suggests calling `<function>(<key path>)` instead.

Example — for
```scss
$colors: (brand: (primary: #D72020), text: (base: #000));
$font-scales: (body: (7: 20px));
```
with
```scss
@function get-color($palette, $tone: 'base') { ... }
@function font-scale($stack, $index) { ... }
```
set:
```json
"variableSuggest.projectMapFunctions": [
  { "variable": "colors", "function": "get-color", "omitTrailingIfEquals": "base" },
  { "variable": "font-scales", "function": "font-scale" }
]
```
Then typing `#D72020` suggests `get-color(brand, primary)`, `#000` suggests `get-color(text)` (trailing `base` omitted since it's the default), and `20px` suggests `font-scale(body, 7)`.
